      "widgets_values": [
        "I added both the Diffusion Model and Unet GGUF Model nodes to the workflow to enable Low VRAM generation if desired. This setup lets you choose between using a standard WAN model or a quantized GGUF model. To use either model, connect the selected node to the Patch Sage Attention KJ node. This node is disabled by default, but it will not disrupt your generations and shoould only be enabled i you have Sage Attention properly installed."
      ],
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1710.2799072265625,
        1213.6099853515625
      ],
      "size": [
        364.0276184082031,
        246.11900329589844
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "I recommend using both the lightx2v and FusionX LoRA models together, as they significantly reduce the required steps and CFG—down to 4/8 steps and CFG 1—resulting in much faster generation times. Using both in tandem at reduced strengths is especially effective, since they complement each other well and can further boost speed without sacrificing quality.\n\nI've also included a WAN detailer LoRA to enhance detail quality in each generation.\n\nI did not personally train these LoRAs but all of these LoRA models are available for download on my Hugging Face page for your convenience:\n\nhttps://huggingface.co/Thelocallab/WAN-2.1-loras/tree/main\n"
      ],
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
